{"statement_id":"BOK_RATE_DECISION_20060407","date":"2006-04-07","rows":[{"text":"The Federal Open Market Committee decided today to raise the target range for the federal funds rate by 1/2 percentage point to 4-1/4 to 4-1/2 percent.","opus55":null,"gemini":null,"deepseek":-6.0,"gpt61sol":null,"ens":-6.0},{"text":"(cid:34)(cid:81)(cid:83)(cid:74)(cid:77)(cid:1) (cid:24)(cid:13)(cid:1) (cid:19)(cid:17)(cid:17)(cid:23)","opus55":null,"gemini":null,"deepseek":null,"gpt61sol":null,"ens":null},{"text":"(cid:53)(cid:73)(cid:70)(cid:1) (cid:35)(cid:66)(cid:79)(cid:76)(cid:1) (cid:80)(cid:71)(cid:1) (cid:44)(cid:80)(cid:83)(cid:70)(cid:66)","opus55":null,"gemini":null,"deepseek":null,"gpt61sol":null,"ens":null},{"text":"The Committee anticipates that ongoing increases in the target range will be appropriate in order to attain a stance of monetary policy that is sufficiently restrictive to return inflation to 2 percent over time.","opus55":null,"gemini":null,"deepseek":-5.0,"gpt61sol":null,"ens":-5.0},{"text":"In determining the pace of future increases in the target range, the Committee will take into account the cumulative tightening of monetary policy, the lags with which monetary policy affects economic activity and inflation, and economic and financial developments.","opus55":null,"gemini":null,"deepseek":0.0,"gpt61sol":null,"ens":0.0},{"text":"(cid:46)(cid:80)(cid:79)(cid:70)(cid:85)(cid:66)(cid:83)(cid:90)(cid:1) (cid:49)(cid:80)(cid:77)(cid:74)(cid:68)(cid:90)(cid:1) (cid:37)(cid:70)(cid:68)(cid:74)(cid:84)(cid:74)(cid:80)(cid:79)","opus55":null,"gemini":null,"deepseek":null,"gpt61sol":null,"ens":null},{"text":"(cid:1) (cid:1) (cid:53)(cid:73)(cid:70)(cid:1) (cid:46)(cid:80)(cid:79)(cid:70)(cid:85)(cid:66)(cid:83)(cid:90)(cid:1) (cid:49)(cid:80)(cid:77)(cid:74)(cid:68)(cid:90)(cid:1) (cid:36)(cid:80)(cid:78)(cid:78)(cid:74)(cid:85)(cid:85)(cid:70)(cid:70)(cid:1) (cid:80)(cid:71)(cid:1) (cid:85)(cid:73)(cid:70)(cid:1) (cid:35)(cid:66)(cid:79)(cid:76)(cid:1) (cid:80)(cid:71)(cid:1) (cid:44)(cid:80)(cid:83)(cid:70)(cid:66)(cid:1) (cid:69)(cid:70)(cid:68)(cid:74)(cid:69)(cid:70)(cid:69)(cid:1)","opus55":null,"gemini":null,"deepseek":null,"gpt61sol":null,"ens":null},{"text":"In addition, the Committee will continue reducing its holdings of Treasury securities and agency debt and agency mortgage-backed securities, as described in its previously announced plans.","opus55":null,"gemini":null,"deepseek":-2.0,"gpt61sol":null,"ens":-2.0},{"text":"(cid:85)(cid:80)(cid:69)(cid:66)(cid:90)(cid:1) (cid:85)(cid:80)(cid:1) (cid:78)(cid:66)(cid:74)(cid:79)(cid:85)(cid:66)(cid:74)(cid:79)(cid:1) (cid:85)(cid:73)(cid:70)(cid:1) (cid:67)(cid:70)(cid:79)(cid:68)(cid:73)(cid:78)(cid:66)(cid:83)(cid:76)(cid:1) (cid:68)(cid:66)(cid:77)(cid:77)(cid:1) (cid:83)(cid:66)(cid:85)(cid:70)(cid:1) (cid:9)(cid:86)(cid:79)(cid:68)(cid:80)(cid:77)(cid:77)(cid:66)(cid:85)(cid:70)(cid:83)(cid:66)(cid:77)(cid:74)(cid:91)(cid:70)(cid:69)(cid:1)","opus55":null,"gemini":null,"deepseek":-2.0,"gpt61sol":null,"ens":-2.0},{"text":"The Committee is strongly committed to returning inflation to its 2 percent objective.","opus55":null,"gemini":null,"deepseek":-4.0,"gpt61sol":null,"ens":-4.0},{"text":"In assessing the appropriate stance of monetary policy, the Committee will continue to monitor the implications of incoming information for the economic outlook.","opus55":null,"gemini":null,"deepseek":0.0,"gpt61sol":null,"ens":0.0},{"text":"(cid:80)(cid:87)(cid:70)(cid:83)(cid:79)(cid:74)(cid:72)(cid:73)(cid:85)(cid:1) (cid:83)(cid:66)(cid:85)(cid:70)(cid:10)(cid:1) (cid:66)(cid:85)(cid:1) (cid:74)(cid:85)(cid:84)(cid:1) (cid:68)(cid:86)(cid:83)(cid:83)(cid:70)(cid:79)(cid:85)(cid:1) (cid:77)(cid:70)(cid:87)(cid:70)(cid:77)(cid:1) (cid:9)(cid:21)(cid:15)(cid:17)(cid:17)(cid:6)(cid:10)(cid:1) (cid:71)(cid:80)(cid:83)(cid:1) (cid:85)(cid:73)(cid:70)(cid:1) (cid:74)(cid:79)(cid:85)(cid:70)(cid:83)(cid:78)(cid:70)(cid:70)(cid:85)(cid:74)(cid:79)(cid:72)(cid:1)","opus55":null,"gemini":null,"deepseek":null,"gpt61sol":null,"ens":null},{"text":"The Committee would be prepared to adjust the stance of monetary policy as appropriate if risks emerge that could impede the attainment of the Committee's goals.","opus55":null,"gemini":null,"deepseek":1.0,"gpt61sol":null,"ens":1.0},{"text":"(cid:81)(cid:70)(cid:83)(cid:74)(cid:80)(cid:69)(cid:15)","opus55":null,"gemini":null,"deepseek":null,"gpt61sol":null,"ens":null},{"text":"(cid:9)(cid:53)(cid:73)(cid:70)(cid:1) (cid:71)(cid:80)(cid:77)(cid:77)(cid:80)(cid:88)(cid:74)(cid:79)(cid:72)(cid:1) (cid:74)(cid:84)(cid:1) (cid:66)(cid:79)(cid:1) (cid:86)(cid:79)(cid:80)(cid:71)(cid:71)(cid:74)(cid:68)(cid:74)(cid:66)(cid:77)(cid:1) (cid:38)(cid:79)(cid:72)(cid:77)(cid:74)(cid:84)(cid:73)(cid:1) (cid:85)(cid:83)(cid:66)(cid:79)(cid:84)(cid:77)(cid:66)(cid:85)(cid:74)(cid:80)(cid:79)(cid:1) (cid:80)(cid:71)(cid:1) (cid:85)(cid:73)(cid:70)(cid:1) (cid:46)(cid:80)(cid:79)(cid:70)(cid:85)(cid:66)(cid:83)(cid:90)(cid:1) (cid:49)(cid:80)(cid:77)(cid:74)(cid:68)(cid:90)(cid:1)","opus55":null,"gemini":null,"deepseek":null,"gpt61sol":null,"ens":null},{"text":"The Committee's assessments will take into account a wide range of information, including readings on public health, labor market conditions, inflation pressures and inflation expectations, and financial and international developments.","opus55":null,"gemini":null,"deepseek":0.0,"gpt61sol":null,"ens":0.0},{"text":"(cid:36)(cid:80)(cid:78)(cid:78)(cid:74)(cid:85)(cid:85)(cid:70)(cid:70)(cid:1) (cid:84)(cid:85)(cid:66)(cid:85)(cid:70)(cid:78)(cid:70)(cid:79)(cid:85)(cid:15)(cid:10)","opus55":null,"gemini":null,"deepseek":null,"gpt61sol":null,"ens":null},{"text":"Voting for the monetary policy action were Jerome H. Powell, Chair; John C. Williams, Vice Chair; Michael S. Barr; Michelle W. Bowman; Lael Brainard; James Bullard; Lisa D. Cook; Esther L. George; Philip N. Jefferson; Loretta J. Mester; and Christopher J. Waller.","opus55":null,"gemini":null,"deepseek":null,"gp